      ],
      "content": "HIGH STREET 1.  5252                                                   (West Side)                                                   Nos 30 to 34 (even)                                                   (The White Hart                                                   Public House) TL 0507 1/25              20.12.67. II                        GV 2. Recorded as The White Hart Inn, 1625.  Early C17, timber framed with red brick rebuilt ground floor.  Old tiled roofs.  2 storeys, lst floor oversailing on moulded beam.  3 sash windows with glazing bars, ground floor 2 light, 1st floor 3 light.  No 34 projects with wide brick gable, 1 sash window, mid C19 shop front with tall slender mullions to 6 arched lights under frieze and cornice.  Carriageway on left of front. Nos 30 to 40 (even) form a group. Listing NGR: TL0555007733"
    }
